  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  name: povray\n  version: \"3.7.0.10\"\n\npackage:\n  name: ${{ name|lower }}\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/POV-Ray/${{ name }}/archive/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 7bee83d9296b98b7956eb94210cf30aa5c1bbeada8ef6b93bb52228bbc83abff\n  patches:\n    # osx-only fixes, adapted from FreeBSD ports (graphics/povray37) and\n    # Homebrew (Formula/p/povray.rb); see the header of each patch for links:\n    # - https://github.com/freebsd/freebsd-ports/commit/6133473e4227abbfcf023bea6ab5eeed9c17e55b\n    # - https://github.com/Homebrew/homebrew-core/blob/master/Formula/p/povray.rb\n    # - https://github.com/POV-Ray/povray/issues/479\n    # libc++ has no std::char_traits<unsigned short>, so the UCS2/UCS4 string\n    # types are built on char16_t/char32_t instead (CPPFLAGS in build.sh).\n    # TARGET_OS_MAC is no longer defined by recent macOS SDKs, which makes\n    # the Fixed typedef clash with MacTypes.h.\n    - if: osx\n      then:\n        - patches/vfe-char16_t.cpp.patch\n        - patches/vfeconf-char16_t.h.patch\n        - patches/truetype-mactypes.patch\n        # osx-arm64 is cross-compiled from osx-64 on CI (build != host);\n        # upstream's configure fails then: AC_RUN_IFELSE-based checks never\n        # pass when cross-compiling\n        - patches/configure-cross-compile.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 3\n  skip: win\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler('cxx') }}\n    - autoconf\n    - automake\n    - make\n  host:\n    - libboost-devel\n    - libpng\n    - libjpeg-turbo\n    - libtiff\n    - zlib\n  run:\n\ntests:\n  - script:\n      - povray --version\n\nabout:\n  license: AGPL-3.0-only\n  license_file: LICENSE\n  summary: The Persistence of Vision Raytracer\n  description: |\n    The Persistence of Vision Raytracer is a high-quality, Free Software\n    tool for creating stunning three-dimensional graphics. The source code\n    is available for those wanting to do their own ports.\n  homepage: http://www.povray.org\n  repository: https://github.com/POV-Ray/povray\n  documentation: http://www.povray.org/documentation/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jan-janssen\n",
